      "text_helper": "Section 36.4.13 \"Timer enable\" in chapter 36 (Low-power timer (LPTIM)), RM0522 Rev 1, page 1495.",
      "section_content": "The ENABLE bit located in the LPTIM_CR register is used to enable/disable the LPTIM\nkernel logic. After setting the ENABLE bit, a delay of two counter clock cycles is needed\nbefore the LPTIM is actually enabled.\nThe LPTIM_CFGR register must be modified only when the LPTIM is disabled.",
